{
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "bosc:provenance": {
    "subject": "QTS \"Van Wert Mega Site\" data-center campus land holding (QTS Van Wert LLC) \u2014 the five Van Wert County parcels deeded to the operator in June 2026, 900.59 ac deeded / 901.502 ac planar, north of U.S. Route 30 between Stripe Road and Mendon Road, Van Wert County OH (FIPS 39161). #1403, sub-issue of #1267.",
    "source": "Van Wert County GIS ArcGIS Online org (vanwertcountygis, G5sGKRBVtJMunpVA) \u2014 parcel_joinedVWOH FeatureServer layer 0 (auditor CAMA + geometry)",
    "source_url": "https://services8.arcgis.com/G5sGKRBVtJMunpVA/arcgis/rest/services/parcel_joinedVWOH/FeatureServer/0",
    "read": "2026-07-31 (the AGOL item's own last-modified is 2026-07-31T03:52Z)",
    "crs": "EPSG:4326 (WGS84)",
    "count": 5,
    "distinct_parcels": 5,
    "parcel_ids": [
      "12-034459.0000",
      "17-034718.0000",
      "17-034718.0100",
      "17-034718.0200",
      "33-047500.0000"
    ],
    "owner_of_record": "QTS VAN WERT LLC",
    "total_cama_acres": 900.59,
    "total_planar_acres": 901.502,
    "caveats": [
      "[verified] Owner of record, deeded acreage, land use/class, appraised values, conveyance date/consideration/type, CAUV flag and the county survey references are verbatim from the Van Wert County Auditor CAMA join (parcel_joinedVWOH layer 0, read 2026-07-31); null means the service had no value. This layer publishes NO owner mailing address and NO legal description, so owner_mailing_address is null on every feature by construction (not an absence in the record) and the deed's legal description is [open].",
      "Assembly membership: QTS VAN WERT LLC owns EXACTLY these five parcels in Van Wert County \u2014 a countywide owner scan (UPPER(PPOwner) LIKE) returns nothing further. Scans for the developer and the intermediate holder return ZERO parcels: 'THOR' matches only unrelated surnames (Thornell/Horstman) and the county Port Authority, and 'FORM8TION', 'VAN WERT EAST' and 'EQUITIES' match nothing at all. In particular VAN WERT EAST OWNER LLC \u2014 the Thor SPE that held the 221.15-ac anchor on the roll as of the 2026-07-10 probe recorded in #1403 \u2014 is gone from the current roll, consistent with the June 2026 conveyance below. No surviving nominee or shell holding was found; that absence is [open], not a negative finding.",
      "GEOMETRY IS DISSOLVED PER PARCEL. The county stores one parcel as several polygon rows (a main body plus slivers); the raw connector pull returns 11 rows for these 5 PINs. Each Feature here is the union of its PIN's rows and gis_row_count records how many were merged. The merge is area-lossless: per parcel the sum of the part areas equals the union area to four decimal places (no overlapping rows).",
      "acres (900.59 total) is the auditor's DEEDED figure; planar_acres (901.502 total) is measured from this geometry in UTM 16N (EPSG:32616), the site's hydro_utm_epsg. The +0.91-ac (0.10%) spread is the deed-vs-GIS difference and is NOT reconciled \u2014 cite the deeded figure for the record and the planar one for area/runoff modeling.",
      "RECONCILIATION AGAINST THE PUBLIC RECORD. The register (data/extracted/van-wert/data-centers.md) carries a 902-acre campus footprint. This recorded holding is 900.59 ac deeded \u2014 0.16% under the quoted campus figure, which corroborates the 902 ac as an ownership-scoped number. \u26a0\ufe0f CORRECTED AGAINST #1401, which landed after this file was written. The annexed and zoned area is 901.698 \u00b1 ac, read off Ordinance 26-05-028's Exhibit A (whose four component acreages sum exactly to the figure printed in both ordinance titles). The \"~962 acres\" this caveat previously reconciled against was a press number with no support anywhere in the record. So the holding is 1.108 ac (0.12%) under the zoned area, NOT \"61.4 ac (6.4%)\" \u2014 and the two explanations that shortfall used to require (road right-of-way inside the annexed area, non-QTS parcels inside the annexation description) are no longer load-bearing at that magnitude. The residual 1.1 ac stays [open] and is still not attributed to right-of-way. The ordinances' legal descriptions ARE now in the corpus (data/extracted/van-wert/mega-site-instruments.yaml). Three independent acreages now agree to within ~1.1 ac: 901.698 zoned, 901.502 planar, 900.59 deeded. The boundary committed here is the recorded OWNERSHIP holding, NOT the annexation boundary and NOT a surveyed earth-disturbance footprint.",
      "TWO CONVEYANCES, AND THE AMOUNTS ARE NOT SUMMED. Four parcels (17-034718.0000, 17-034718.0200, 33-047500.0000, 12-034459.0000 \u2014 679.44 ac) carry the SAME date 2026-06-16 and the SAME consideration $39,117,825; a single multi-parcel deed whose consideration the auditor repeats on each parcel is the ordinary reading, so that figure is recorded verbatim per parcel and deliberately NOT added across them ([inference] \u2014 the deed itself is [open]). The anchor 17-034718.0100 (221.15 ac) is separate: 2026-06-18, $110,575,000, which is EXACTLY $500,000 x its 221.15 CAMA acres. Both are type WD (warranty deed). The GRANTOR is [open] on every one \u2014 this layer carries no grantor field and no deed book/page, so the Marsh Foundation -> Thor/Form8tion -> QTS chain is not closed by this dataset; the Van Wert County Recorder instruments are the pull (#1401).",
      "The price step is on the record and is not explained by it. The anchor's prior sale \u2014 $10,394,000 for the same 221.15 ac on 2025-08-22, i.e. ~$47,000/ac \u2014 is [reference] to the 2026-07-10 roll probe recorded in #1403 and is NO LONGER on the live layer (the June 2026 conveyance superseded it), so it is not re-verified here. Against it the June 2026 $500,000/ac is a 10.6x step in ten months on the same parcel.",
      "TAX DISTRICT: the auditor's district is the PIN's leading two digits, and all five parcels are in Van Wert CORPORATION districts (12, 17, 33) per the county's own TaxDistrict table \u2014 while that layer's POLYGON geometry still places all five in TOWNSHIPS (11-Pleasant Twp. (VW), 19-Ridge Twp, 15-Hoaglin Twp.), carried per feature as tax_district_gis_layer. That is a currency gap in the published polygons, not a contradiction: the roll is the current record. District 33 is absent from the district table entirely (it stops at 32) and has EXACTLY ONE parcel countywide \u2014 33-047500.0000, this assemblage's Hoaglin Township tract \u2014 so it is a district created after that layer's vintage, which is why tax_district is null there. Reading the corporation-district placement as the effect of the 2026-05-11 annexation is [inference], and it STAYS [inference] now that the ordinances ARE committed (#1401, data/extracted/van-wert/mega-site-instruments.yaml): none of the three recites a tax district, so the roll's district assignment and the ordinances' legal descriptions are separate records and neither cites the other.",
      "THE ASSEMBLAGE STRADDLES TWO SCHOOL DISTRICTS, which the register did not have. 772.46 ac (four parcels) are Lincolnview and 128.13 ac (12-034459.0000) is Van Wert City \u2014 so the register's [reference] 'property taxes flow to Lincolnview Local School District' is incomplete, and a CRA school-compensation agreement would have to reach both boards. Two independent lines agree for the four: the auditor's own district name carries the '(LV)' suffix (17-Van Wert Corp.-Ridge Twp. (LV)) and the county SchoolDistrict layer returns Lincolnview at each parcel's interior point. For 33-047500.0000 only the spatial join is available (no district-table row), and for 12-034459.0000 the '12-Van Wert Corp.' district and the layer agree on Van Wert City.",
      "Two parcels are UNVALUED, not valueless: 17-034718.0200 (157.84 ac) and 12-034459.0000 (128.13 ac) carry null appraised land/improvement/total values and a null CAUV flag \u2014 new splits the auditor had not valued at this extract. Read null as 'not yet valued', never $0.",
      "NO CAMPUS IMPROVEMENT IS ON THE TAX RECORD. The only improvement value in the assemblage is $25,580 on 17-034718.0000, with year_built 1900 and CAMA grade C \u2014 a pre-existing farm structure, not data-center construction. 17-034718.0200 carries the same year_built 1900 with NO improvement value: a split parcel inheriting the parent's building attributes, which is a CAMA artifact and not a second structure. Groundbreaking is planned for Q4 2026.",
      "class is the coarse CAMA class LETTER (A = agricultural) and land_use_code is the numeric Ohio use code (110 / 199). This layer publishes no use-code NAME, so none is asserted here.",
      "survey_reference / prior_survey_reference are the Van Wert County Engineer survey-record filenames the CAMA carries (VW-SD522-1.pdf, VW-SD522-2.pdf, VW-SD522-523.pdf, VW-SD524.pdf; priors T1S R3E Section 31 / T2S R2E Section 01 / T2S R3E Section 06). They name the split surveys that created these parcels out of the Marsh Foundation tract and are the most specific instrument locator this layer offers. The survey documents themselves are NOT in the corpus. [open]",
      "FEMA Zone A (SFHA) covers 15.62 ac of the 901.5-ac assemblage (1.7%), per the county's own FloodPlain layer intersected with this geometry. [verified] as the county's published mapping; the site's authoritative floodzone connector is the national NFHL layer.",
      "Adjacent leads, deliberately EXCLUDED (not QTS-owned, no instrument ties them to the campus): the Marsh Foundation still holds 19-041272.0000 (200.83 ac, Stripe Rd, ~69 m from this boundary across Stripe Road), 12-031248.0200 (93.62 ac) and 12-031252.0000 (49.35 ac). Reading those as the remainder of the register's ~1,500-ac Mega Site is [inference]. No parcel that actually adjoins this assemblage is Marsh- or QTS-owned \u2014 the 26 abutters are farm and residential holdings (VanWynsberghe, Germann, Doner, Cooper Hatchery, the Kriegel trust, the County Port Authority's 3.29-ac Marsh Rd parcel)."
    ]
  },
